<title>POLAND: Polish wheat, barley prices inch up in July 1-7.</title>
<headline>Polish wheat, barley prices inch up in July 1-7.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish wheat and barley prices inched up at grain auctions in June 30-July 7 for the second week running while rye prices held flat, the Polish Agriculture Ministry said in a statement</p>
<p>POLISH FARM AUCTION PRICES (AVERAGE)</p>
<p>Product  week to July 7 previous week  week/week  yr/yr change</p>
<p>  Wheat     52 zl/q	 52 zl/q	   0.6 pct    -18.4 pct</p>
<p>  Rye	 40 zl/q	 40 zl/q	   0.0 pct     -5.6 pct</p>
<p>  Barley    47 zl/q	 46 zl/q	   0.2 pct    -18.4 pct</p>
<p>NOTE: zl/q = zlotys per quintal.</p>
<p>--Warsaw Newsroom+48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
